In article <1991Oct14.150100.20476@cbnewsl.cb.att.com>, wjb@moss.ATT.COM writes...
>Miscellaneous questions not in the FAQ file:
    As spoilers go, these don't rate very high, but...

>1) statistically, what works out better, a cloak of displacement or a cloak
>of protection?
     I'll pass on this one.  I think the consensus is that displacement
is much better, because you can always get shear AC points elsewhere.
An AC below 0 actually fluctuates randomly between 0 and AC, so each
point in the negative range is only worth about 50% (on the average)
compared to non-negative AC.

>2) does a cloak of protection protect against magic?
     No; if it did, why would the cloak of magic protection even exist?
You could just start a game in explore mode and wish for the cloak and a
potion of enlightenment (or the cloak and just Q[uit], for that matter).

>3) what keystrokes do you use to give a priest a given amount of money?
     #chat, then answer the questions, pretty much like with the Oracle.

>4) if there is no priest in an altar room when I first arrive, is there a
>way to summon one?
     No.  Priests only occur in temples, not with ordinary altars.  What
makes a temple special?  It starts with a priest in it.  ;-)

